    "verseCount": 7,
    "content": "<p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"1\" data-sid=\"PSA 119:1\" class=\"v\">1</span>In my trouble I cried to the Lord: and he heard me.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"2\" data-sid=\"PSA 119:2\" class=\"v\">2</span>O Lord, deliver my soul from wicked lips, and a deceitful tongue.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"3\" data-sid=\"PSA 119:3\" class=\"v\">3</span>What shall be given to thee, or what shall be added to thee, to a deceitful tongue.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"4\" data-sid=\"PSA 119:4\" class=\"v\">4</span>The sharp arrows of the mighty, with coals that lay waste.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"5\" data-sid=\"PSA 119:5\" class=\"v\">5</span>Woe is me, that my sojourning is prolonged! I have dwelt with the inhabitants of cedar:</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"6\" data-sid=\"PSA 119:6\" class=\"v\">6</span>My soul hath been long a sojourner.</p><p class=\"q1\"><span data-number=\"7\" data-sid=\"PSA 119:7\" class=\"v\">7</span>With them that hate peace I was peaceable: when I spoke to them they fought against me without cause.</p>",
